  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - he development shall be carried out in accordance with the reports, specifications and drawings detailed [Accommodation Schedule (doc. ref. C05-DFA-RS6A-XX-A-SA-00-00001) dated 05/12/2025; Battersea Phase 5A - Alignment with Passivhaus principles, no date, by DFA; Cover letter, dated 09/12/2025, by DP9; Design and Access Statement, dated December 2025, by Dowen Farmer Architects; Drainage Strategy (doc. ref. C05-BH-RS6A-XX-RP-C-10-0001) rev. P01, dated 19/11/2026, by Buro Happold; EIA Further Information Review Report, dated December 2025, by Quod; Heritage Impact Assessment Addendum, dated 24/11/2025, by Roger Mears Architects; Landscape Statement, dated 28/11/2025, by Camlins; Planning Statement, dated December 2025, by DP9; Response to comments from the Owners of Brooks Court, dated 24/03/2026, by DP9; Response to comments from Western Riverside Waste Authority (WRWA), dated 24/03/2026, by DP9; Response to Ecology Comments, undated, by Camlins; Response to Port of London Authority (PLA) Comments, dated 24/03/2026, by DP9; Response to Public Comments from Riverlight Quay, dated 24/03/2026, by DP9; Response to representations on behalf of Thames Water, dated 11/08/2026, by DP9; Statement of Community Involvement, dated December 2025, by Cascade Communications; Statement of Compliance, dated December 2025, by DP9; Technical Note Response to LBW Waste Comments (doc. ref. 25381-TN01-1A) rev. 1A, dated 18/03/2026; Technical Note Response to LBW Waste Comments (doc. ref. 25381-TN01-1A) rev. 1A, dated 18/03/2026, by Markides Associates; Technical Note Response to The Battersea Society (doc. ref. 25381-TN01-1A) rev. 1A, dated 13/03/2026, by Markides Associates; Technical Note Response to Transport for London (doc. ref. 25381-TN01-1A) rev. 1A, dated 18/03/2026, by Markides Associates; C05-DFA-RS6A-00-A-DR-11-0000 P01 (GA Plan - Level 00); C05-DFA-RS6A-01-A-DR-11-0001 P01 (GA Plan - Level 01); C05-DFA-RS6A-02-A-DR-11-0002 P01 (GA Plan - Level 02); C05-DFA-RS6A-03-A-DR-11-00",
    "Condition : 2 - Prior to the commencement of development, a Dust Management Plan (DMP), based on an AQDRA (Air Quality and Dust Risk Assessment), shall be submitted to and approved, in writing, by the local planning authority. The DMP shall be in accordance with The Control of Dust and Emissions during Construction and Demolition SPG 2014. The DMP will need to detail the measures to reduce the impacts during the construction phase. The development shall be undertaken in accordance with the approved plan.\r\nReason: To manage and prevent further deterioration of existing low quality air across London in accordance with Local Plan policy LP14 and London Plan policy SI1.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - During each of the four construction sub-phases of the proposed development (demolition, earthworks, construction, and trackout), PM10 continuous monitoring shall be carried out on site. Parameters to be monitored, duration, locations and monitoring techniques must be approved in writing by Wandsworth Council prior to commencement of monitoring. \r\nReason: To manage and prevent further deterioration of existing low quality air across London in accordance with London Plan policy SI1.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to commencement of above ground works, a revised highway works design, including site levels, shall be submitted to and be approved in writing by the Borough Engineer and Transport for London. The revised highway works shall include:\r\na)\tThe provision of inset bays to accommodate inset disabled parking and/or loading bays on the southern side of Cringle Street north of the development.\r\nb)\tThe adoption of 1.8m of usable footway space by the Council as Local Highway Authority on the southern side of Cringle Street north of the site.\r\nc)\tA revised Traffic Management Order to enable the installation of 6 disabled parking bays and up to two loading only bays on Kirtling Street and/or Cringle Street fronting the development and amendments to the zig zag lining on the east of Kirtling Street south of the Zebra crossing.\r\nFollowing the completion of an agreement under S38/278 of the Highways Act 1980, the approved highway works shall then be completed in accordance with the approved details to the satisfaction of the Borough Engineer before first occupation of Phase 5A. \r\nReason: In the interest of highway safety, to ensure that the pavement is made safe, and to provide additional on-street parking space in accordance with Council policies LP2 and LP51 of the Local Plan coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to the completion of the ground floor slab, a report following a 6-month baseline monitoring period through NO2 diffusion tubes shall be submitted to and approved, in writing, by the local planning authority. Locations and methodology of monitoring shall be agreed by the Wandsworth Council prior to commencement of monitoring. The baseline monitoring report will establish whether a scheme of proposed air quality mitigation measures to protect the future occupiers from air pollution exposure shall be submitted to the local planning authority. \r\nReason: To protect the internal amenity of future occupants of the development in accordance with policy LP2 and LP14 of the Local Plan.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - Notwithstanding the details set out in the Fire Statement for Phase 5A submitted pursuant to condition 84 of 2021/0414, further details are required to meet the remaining requirements of London Plan policies D5 and D12. Prior to first occupation, details of evacuation and management procedures shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. \r\nThe development shall thereafter be completed and maintained in accordance with the approved details, unless otherwise agreed in writing.\r\nReason: To ensure that adequate arrangements are made for fire safety in accordance with Local Plan policy LP27 and London Plan policies D5 and D12.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - Notwithstanding the details in the approved documents, prior to the implementation of any landscaping scheme and features, a tree species planting plan and timescales for implementation shall be submitted to and be approved in writing by the local planning authority. This shall include details of the expected maximum height of each tree species and the spread of their root systems. The tree planting shall therefore be carried out in accordance with the agreed timescales and thereafter maintained in accordance with the approved details.\r\nReason: In the interest of design quality and visual amenity in accordance with Local Plan policies LP1 and LP56.\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - Notwithstanding the details shown on the approved plans and as set out in the supporting documents, prior to the occupation of the development details of the play space, equipment and street furniture shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. This shall include details of the management and maintenance of the playspace, including measures to ensure surface and equipment meet relevant British Standards, full details of the regular inspection and maintenance programme to be implemented to ensure access, safety and the anticipated life span before replacement is maintained. Prior to the occupation of the development, the playspace shall be implemented and provided in accordance with the approved details and retained thereafter for the lifetime of the development, unless otherwise approved in writing by the local planning authority. \r\nReason: To provide public access to play and recreation facilities in accordance with Local Plan policies LP19 and LP20 and to meet the requirements for the provision of play and informal recreation for children and young people in accordance with London Plan policy S4.\r\n",
    "Condition : 9 - The original design team (including the architects and landscape designers) shall be retained to assist in the detailed design of the exterior of the development and to monitor the design quality of the development through to completion, including the landscaping, unless otherwise approved in writing by the local planning authority. \r\nReason: To maintain the design quality of the development through to the completion of the development, in the interest of the visual amenity of the area, in accordance with London Plan policy D4. \r\n",
    "Condition : 10 - Prior to first occupation of the development hereby permitted, an Environmental Amenity Policy Statement (EAPS) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.\r\nThe EAPS shall provide information for all future occupiers on the environmental conditions associated with the occupation of the development, including:\r\na)\tthe presence and operation of nearby Safeguarded Wharves and the role they perform within London's safeguarded wharf network;\r\nb)\tthe potential for noise, dust and odour associated with the lawful operation of the Safeguarded Wharves, including activities that may occur during daytime, evening and night-time periods;\r\nc)\tthe design and mitigation measures incorporated into the development to minimise the effects of external noise, including the purpose and operation of any acoustic glazing, mechanical ventilation and other mitigation measures;\r\nd)\tguidance on the appropriate use and operation of these mitigation measures to maintain internal acoustic conditions; and\r\ne)\tcontact details for the building management responsible for maintenance of the acoustic mitigation measures.\r\nThe approved EAPS shall be provided to the first occupier of each dwelling prior to or upon first occupation and shall be made available to all subsequent occupiers of the dwelling for the lifetime of the development.\r\nThe development shall thereafter be managed in accordance with the approved details.\r\nReason: To protect the amenities of occupants, in accordance with policies LP2 and LP14 of the Local Plan.\r\n",
    "Condition : 11 - Prior to occupation of the development, the windows annotated on the approved drawings to have obscure glazing, shall be obscure-glazed and non-opening (unless the parts of the window which can be opened are more than 1.7m above the floor of the room in which the window is installed). The windows shall so be maintained and retained as such. \r\nReason: To control overlooking and safeguard the privacy of neighbours in accordance with Council policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n",
    "Condition : 12 - All non-road mobile machinery (NRMM) used during the course of the development that is within the scope of the Greater London Authority 'Control of Dust and Emissions during Construction and Demolition' Supplementary Planning Guidance (SPG) dated July 2014, or any subsequent amendment or guidance, shall comply with the emission requirements therein. \r\nReason: To manage and prevent further deterioration of existing low quality air across London in accordance with Local Plan policy LP14 and London Plan policy SI1.\r\n",
    "Condition : 13 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (or any Order revoking, amending or re-enacting that Order) no satellite dishes, telecommunications masts, antennas or equipment or associated structures, shall be installed on the building hereby approved, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority. \r\nReason: To protect the appearance of the building, and accord with Council policies LP1, LP2 and LP22 of the Local Plan coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n",
    "Condition : 14 - No water tanks, plant, lift rooms or other permanent structures (unless otherwise shown on the approved plans listed above) shall be erected upon the roof of the approved building unless otherwise agreed in writing with the local planning authority.\r\nReason: To control the appearance of the building and safeguard the appearance of the area, in accordance with Local Plan policy LP1 coupled with the requirements of the National Planning Policy Framework.\r\n\r\n"
  ],
